---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { PAGES } from "../lib/site";
---
<Base {...PAGES.members} nav="members">
<!-- ============ PAGE HERO ============ -->
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="kicker">Coalition &amp; Members</span>
    <h1 style="margin-top:16px;">A coalition of organizations that don't work alone.</h1>
    <p class="lede">The Youth Justice Project is a voluntary alliance of DC youth defenders, legal advocates, and allied organizations. Each keeps its own independent voice and mandate. Together, they coordinate the work no single organization can carry alone.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ MEMBERS ============ -->
<section class="section-sm">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="shead">
      <span class="kicker">Member organizations</span>
      <h2>Who makes up the coalition.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="member-grid">
      <div class="member-card">
        <div class="mhead"><h3>Open City Advocates</h3><span class="macro">OCA</span></div>
        <p>Provides youth-centered legal defense and holistic advocacy for young people after sentencing in the DC juvenile legal system, and works for systemic improvements to the juvenile legal system, both locally and nationally, to better the lives of marginalized children and youth.</p>
        <a class="mlink" href="https://opencityadvocates.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">opencityadvocates.org</a>
      </div>
      <div class="member-card">
        <div class="mhead"><h3>School Justice Project</h3><span class="macro">SJP</span></div>
        <p>Uses special education law to ensure that older, court-involved students with disabilities have access to a quality education, both during incarceration and throughout reentry.</p>
        <a class="mlink" href="https://sjpdc.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">sjpdc.org</a>
      </div>
      <div class="member-card">
        <div class="mhead"><h3>Free Minds Book Club &amp; Writing Workshop</h3><span class="macro">Free Minds</span></div>
        <p>Builds community to foster personal development and systems change for incarcerated and formerly incarcerated youth and adults through the literary arts, workforce development, trauma healing, peace-building, and member-led advocacy.</p>
        <a class="mlink" href="https://freemindsbookclub.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">freemindsbookclub.org</a>
      </div>
      <div class="member-card">
        <div class="mhead"><h3>Washington Lawyers' Committee for Civil Rights and Urban Affairs</h3><span class="macro">WLC</span></div>
        <p>Works to create legal, economic, and social equity, primarily through strategic litigation and related public policy advocacy. WLC partners with individuals and communities facing discrimination and with the legal community to achieve justice.</p>
        <a class="mlink" href="https://washlaw.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">washlaw.org</a>
      </div>
      <div class="member-card">
        <div class="mhead"><h3>DC Justice Lab</h3><span class="macro">DCJL</span></div>
        <p>A team of law and policy experts researching, organizing, and advocating for large-scale changes to the District of Columbia's criminal legal system. DC Justice Lab develops smarter safety solutions that are evidence-driven, community-rooted, and racially just.</p>
        <a class="mlink" href="https://dcjusticelab.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">dcjusticelab.org</a>
      </div>
      <div class="member-card">
        <div class="mhead"><h3>Disability Rights DC at University Legal Services</h3><span class="macro">DRDC</span></div>
        <p>The federally designated Protection and Advocacy Program for persons with disabilities in the District of Columbia. DRDC staff serve the District's residents with disabilities through individual representation, investigations of abuse and neglect, education and training, and systemic advocacy.</p>
        <a class="mlink" href="https://uls-dc.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">uls-dc.org</a>
      </div>
      <div class="member-card">
        <div class="mhead"><h3>Council for Court Excellence</h3><span class="macro">CCE</span></div>
        <p>Founded in 1982, CCE is an independent, nonprofit organization that brings people together to conduct research, educate, and advocate in order to make DC's legal systems more just, equitable, and accountable to the community. CCE envisions a DC where individuals, organizations, and government work together to build safe and thriving communities with a trusted legal system that meets the needs of its people, protects their rights, and promotes dignity and justice for all.</p>
        <a class="mlink" href="https://www.courtexcellence.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">courtexcellence.org</a>
      </div>
      <div class="member-card">
        <div class="mhead"><h3>D.C. Juvenile Bar Association</h3><span class="macro">JBA</span></div>
        <p>Founded in July 2026, the JBA is a professional association of the D.C. Criminal Justice Act Juvenile Delinquency Panel and Post-Commitment Panel attorneys who practice before the Superior Court and the Court of Appeals. It represents the interests of juvenile defense attorneys, works to maintain and improve the quality of legal services for children and families, and takes positions on legislation, regulations, court rules, and other policy matters affecting its members and their clients.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="note-strip">Listing as a coalition member organization does not mean that every member endorses every coalition position. Shared positions reflect consensus at the time they are adopted, and members may decline to join individual positions while remaining members of the coalition.</p>

    <!-- HOW WE OPERATE -->
    <div class="join-band" id="operate" style="margin-top:52px;">
      <div>
        <span class="kicker">How we operate</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top:14px;">No staff. No steering committee. Decisions by consensus.</h3>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>The Youth Justice Project has no staff and no steering committee. Member organizations make decisions together by consensus. Open City Advocates serves as the coalition's administrative backbone, providing meeting coordination, recordkeeping, and logistics, with no special voting authority.</p>
        <p>The coalition is an unincorporated nonprofit association under DC Code § 29–1102 and a legal entity distinct from any of its member organizations. It does not represent individual clients or provide legal advice.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- HISTORY -->
    <div class="history-band" id="history">
      <span class="kicker">Since 2010</span>
      <h3>Where we come from.</h3>
      <p class="hintro">The Youth Justice Project launched in 2010 to advance a proactive, long-term youth justice agenda in the District of Columbia.</p>
      <div class="history-rail">
        <div class="era">
          <span class="era-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="era-years">2010&ndash;2018</div>
          <div class="era-title">Founded by DC Lawyers for Youth</div>
          <p class="era-sum">Launched with the support of the Public Welfare Foundation and nine original member organizations. DC Lawyers for Youth provided administrative support until 2018.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="era">
          <span class="era-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="era-years">2018&ndash;2025</div>
          <div class="era-title">Georgetown Law's Juvenile Justice Clinic &amp; Initiative</div>
          <p class="era-sum">Supported the coalition from 2018 to 2025.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="era">
          <span class="era-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <div class="era-years">2025&ndash;</div>
          <div class="era-title">Open City Advocates</div>
          <p class="era-sum">Assumed administrative responsibility for the coalition.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- JOIN -->
    <div class="join-band">
      <div>
        <span class="kicker">Join the coalition</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top:14px;">Interested in becoming a member?</h3>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>The Youth Justice Project admits new member organizations by consensus of current members. If your organization works on DC youth justice and wants to explore membership, write to <a class="email" href="mailto:joshua@opencityadvocates.org,kyla@opencityadvocates.org" style="color:var(--anchor); font-weight:600;">joshua@opencityadvocates.org</a> with a short description of your organization and your interest. We will share the Charter and the membership process with you.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
